            {
                "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                "word": "rognon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bbb2ec35-0d34-48cb-b487-22eed8fafe90",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "rognons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rein d’un animal, en parlant de certains animaux dont les reins sont bons à manger."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b6dcd3b-e247-49e0-9b93-c34323c3435a",
                                "sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                                "text": "Rognons de veau, de bœuf, de mouton à la brochette."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3edc21e-2e7e-4c84-b171-defa3d592898",
                                "sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                                "text": "Le lendemain, après une route de quatre lieues, nous déjeunâmes avec des filets de bœuf, des côtelettes de mouton, des rognons sautés, de la salade et du vin de Champagne dans la petite ville de Pont-Croix."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67924f7a-6d11-4d97-aecb-0f11159fe82c",
                                "sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                                "text": "Son gigot, sa morue, ses rognons qui puaient la pisse, ses gélatines qui flageolaient comme les cuisses de MaryAnn, ça me soulevait le cœur."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "959ac12d-0b35-33f6-b49e-4f7a50ec0ba0",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Testicules d’animaux, animelles, daintiers ou rognons blancs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8edd26e3-8ce6-42fe-a93a-bcaba4fe15c4",
                                "sense_id": "959ac12d-0b35-33f6-b49e-4f7a50ec0ba0",
                                "text": "Daintiers : Ce sont les rognons (testicules) du cerf"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c25cbe2-86a7-488f-b4ac-b4885a1da67d",
                                "sense_id": "959ac12d-0b35-33f6-b49e-4f7a50ec0ba0",
                                "text": "Des rognons de coq ou testicules de coq."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6f102c3-93e1-46c7-b8d5-d63664373d50",
                                "sense_id": "959ac12d-0b35-33f6-b49e-4f7a50ec0ba0",
                                "text": "Les «rognons blancs» désignent les testicules de taureaux, d'agneau ou de bélier. On les appelle aussi «animelles»."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90f0d00e-af6c-34e7-bbb7-d927bd11b675",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Testicule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b6c34d3-7eb7-4103-acb2-e66f9fd51a05",
                                "sense_id": "90f0d00e-af6c-34e7-bbb7-d927bd11b675",
                                "text": "Ce n'est pas un jeu, rétorquai-je en esquivant, avant de lui flanquer coup dans les rognons avec ces nunchakus d'entraînement suffisamment inoffensifs pour ne pas briser les os , mais pas assez pour être indolores."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a43c604-5f83-3b7a-bf8b-e6816ef7b402",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Roche enrobée dans un minéral de nature différente."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "166314b4-8686-455c-9f35-d7389c967e65",
                                "sense_id": "4a43c604-5f83-3b7a-bf8b-e6816ef7b402",
                                "text": "Mine en rognons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a9af219-7df8-4feb-9b40-bca9ab25569f",
                                "sense_id": "4a43c604-5f83-3b7a-bf8b-e6816ef7b402",
                                "text": "Ce monsieur est un personnage qui fait une collection de cailloux et a cherché partout un rognon.\nJ’ai entendu parler de ce rognon pendant six mois, toujours avec le même étonnement ; à la fin on a trouvé une chose couleur de fer, que mon père a empaquetée avec soin et que je dois porter au collectionneur ; il est parent de je ne sais plus qui dans la haute Université, et la fortune professionnelle de mon père peut s’accrocher à ce rognon.\nCe mot de rognon me gêne tout de même, et quand une dame, qui se trouve là au moment où je déboucle ma malle, demande ce que c’est que ce caillou bleu, je ne lui dis pas comment on l’appelle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af420737-63f4-4a56-b6b7-6ef8d2d71e88",
                                "sense_id": "4a43c604-5f83-3b7a-bf8b-e6816ef7b402",
                                "text": "Saussure saute à terre et pendant plus d’une heure étudie la structure géologique de l’île. Mais que de schistes argileux mêlés de rognons et de feuillets de quartz ! Que de roches schisteuses aux feuillets bien parallèles !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e2be448-b2bd-33eb-9551-4b8168c0a3bb",
                        "entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petite table, dont le plateau, parfois entouré d'un rebord en saillie, affecte la forme stylisée d'un rognon (la même qu'un haricot). — Une table rognon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "En apposition"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b76541d-6efa-4996-8f7f-0b8e5d942fd9",
                                "sense_id": "5e2be448-b2bd-33eb-9551-4b8168c0a3bb",
                                "text": "Enfin, quand il s'éveille, prend-il du café, ou non?\n— Oui. Pose la tasse sur le rognon."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "efd2cc12-1ac3-4fa1-bc7a-7c9001a07655",
                        "source_entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "source_sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Cuisine) Rein d’un animal",
                        "target_lang_word": "kidney",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kidney",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8982d0e5-12c4-30d8-a4bf-bb992fd17a42",
                                        "entry_id": "9ad041f8-018e-349d-abcc-58746ee7eee2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An organ in the body that filters the blood, producing urine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e422ed4-2b24-4db0-a2dd-732fc0d7ff86",
                                                "sense_id": "8982d0e5-12c4-30d8-a4bf-bb992fd17a42",
                                                "text": "The liver and the kidneys of animals have long been gastronomically popular for their aphrodisiac properties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bc39b1a-e94d-43d3-b741-b0f77c80ca51",
                                                "sense_id": "8982d0e5-12c4-30d8-a4bf-bb992fd17a42",
                                                "text": "An artificial kidney these days still means a refrigerator-sized dialysis machine. Such devices mimic the way real kidneys cleanse blood and eject impurities and surplus water as urine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "468b1578-4b26-3818-b3ce-63ad9830083f",
                                        "entry_id": "9ad041f8-018e-349d-abcc-58746ee7eee2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "This organ (of an animal) cooked as food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fb830b5-1f43-3dc0-93f5-94f4445b84da",
                                        "entry_id": "9ad041f8-018e-349d-abcc-58746ee7eee2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Constitution, temperament, nature, type, character, disposition. (usually used of people)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4ae452b-2752-4888-b156-a3a2f917bf01",
                                                "sense_id": "6fb830b5-1f43-3dc0-93f5-94f4445b84da",
                                                "text": "[…] think of that, – a man of my kidney, – think of that, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f59d930-398a-4153-8909-7e07f685590e",
                                                "sense_id": "6fb830b5-1f43-3dc0-93f5-94f4445b84da",
                                                "text": "Millions in the World of this Man's Kidney"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7c965a7-bd81-4ba7-ba99-f74ea001ee22",
                                                "sense_id": "6fb830b5-1f43-3dc0-93f5-94f4445b84da",
                                                "text": "30th June, 1788, Robert Burns, letter to Mr Robert Ainslie\nYour poets, spendthrifts, and other fools of that kidney, pretend, forsooth, to crack their jokes on prudence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1861e761-bbcb-43cb-851f-f17cdf40c70e",
                                                "sense_id": "6fb830b5-1f43-3dc0-93f5-94f4445b84da",
                                                "text": "I shall not want Honour in Heaven\n For I shall meet Sir Philip Sidney\nAnd have talk with Coriolanus\n And other heroes of that kidney."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0a1a4db-920a-335a-aa1b-ace71aa3be81",
                                        "entry_id": "9ad041f8-018e-349d-abcc-58746ee7eee2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A waiter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "697afd2b-da10-47c4-93b1-f376e0370703",
                                                "sense_id": "e0a1a4db-920a-335a-aa1b-ace71aa3be81",
                                                "text": "I once more desire my readers to consider that as I cannot keep an ingenious man to go daily to Will's under twopence each day merely for his charges, to White's under sixpence, nor to the Grecian without allowing him some plain Spanish, to be as able as others at the learned table; and that a good observer cannot speak with even Kidney at St. James's without clean linen; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fad91e07-045c-4ed0-92cd-85e83cf7cecc",
                        "source_entry_id": "b1f1b6ec-a5c8-3b00-9979-e95666e1883b",
                        "source_sense_id": "730217b4-28fd-3380-8281-cd4145645cf5",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Cuisine) Rein d’un animal",
                        "target_lang_word": "liver",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "liver",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14f7626f-49d0-3582-bee7-28141d5ee683",
                                        "entry_id": "dea8aa31-b394-3723-a6c6-b0c449e84b3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large organ in the body that stores and metabolizes nutrients, destroys toxins and produces bile. It is responsible for thousands of biochemical reactions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c37b00d-d7c6-45e4-bff6-6fd9d5cef106",
                                                "sense_id": "14f7626f-49d0-3582-bee7-28141d5ee683",
                                                "text": "Steve Jobs is a famous liver transplant recipient."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfeca577-eb43-3bf6-885a-b01cbb0b5622",
                                        "entry_id": "dea8aa31-b394-3723-a6c6-b0c449e84b3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "This organ, as taken from animals used as food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97ddd6a2-262e-4ffa-a194-650c240a1614",
                                                "sense_id": "bfeca577-eb43-3bf6-885a-b01cbb0b5622",
                                                "text": "I'd like some goose liver pate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f211f549-5e91-4a80-9b8d-2412f98efe54",
                                                "sense_id": "bfeca577-eb43-3bf6-885a-b01cbb0b5622",
                                                "text": "You could fry up some chicken livers for a tasty treat. — Nah, I don't like chicken liver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0554a65d-00bb-4f9b-82ea-5b1e1265707b",
                                                "sense_id": "bfeca577-eb43-3bf6-885a-b01cbb0b5622",
                                                "text": "\"I should think you've rocked the boat enough already by refusing to eat liver.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "535f5256-462b-3047-b4f8-b4c5ed6ed6b3",
                                        "entry_id": "dea8aa31-b394-3723-a6c6-b0c449e84b3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dark brown colour, tinted with red and gray, like the colour of liver."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d61076da-29a1-3688-8b36-c17925f7650b",
                                        "entry_id": "dea8aa31-b394-3723-a6c6-b0c449e84b3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various chemical compounds—particularly sulfides—thought to resemble livers in color."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd4732b8-5e5f-4acd-afd6-eb78f3fb8828",
                                                "sense_id": "d61076da-29a1-3688-8b36-c17925f7650b",
                                                "text": "He gave his horse some liver of antimony."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "liver",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "795d966d-a6df-3117-8a37-142720db65c8",
                                        "entry_id": "cdf15a3b-951a-3889-85c9-da3916741bd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the colour of liver (dark brown, tinted with red and gray)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca59ee70-06ee-40f2-ad05-64472f36f218",
                                                "sense_id": "795d966d-a6df-3117-8a37-142720db65c8",
                                                "text": "His friend Rothwell, who had the use of the best Laveracks for breeding purposes, wrote him that one of his puppies was liver and white."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "liver",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                        "entry_id": "8e979316-3c22-3178-b7bc-d764bfd7fc14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who lives (usually in a specified way)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d999e1d-68fa-47a2-92aa-929b7a23d568",
                                                "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                                "text": "Ephori of Sparta, hearing a dissolute liver propose a very beneficial advise unto the people, commaunded him to hold his peace, and desired an honest man to assume the invention of it unto himselfe and to propound it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f55a7bc5-2a34-4aed-a56b-a7cacba17bfb",
                                                "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                                "text": "a wicked liver may be reclaimed, and prove an honest man[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65324381-028d-4f78-b0c5-3aeb0c791e43",
                                                "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                                "text": "Try if life be worth the liver's care."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63023135-6c43-42b2-bc40-f620e5ab0f2a",
                                                "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                                "text": "[…] a stately speech; / Such as grave Livers do in Scotland use, / Religious men, who give to God and Man their dues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19033c0e-f7df-463c-aab9-7deef18676a9",
                                                "sense_id": "5e95512a-80ae-3354-b3cd-14d4d54cdd03",
                                                "text": "A great lover of the faith, a great defender of the faith, a great lover of life, great liver of life, great defender of life. And yet he plotted and planned over fifty murders, and carried each of one them out—if only on paper, and if only for our pleasure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
